    "readComparability": "every subject that can decode the table is ranked, because the server sends identical bytes to all of them; proven decode losses are the int64 and nanosecond checks in `fidelity`, while `roundTripUnverifiedSubjects` records only that the decode-then-encode round trip could not be proven, which the encoder alone can cause",
